From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmd: Tab completes file and directory names

Issue #14 (live ISO): Tab in cmd put a tab character (^I) in the line. As
Windows' cmd does, Tab now completes the word before the cursor to the
first file or directory name that starts with it, Tab again to the next,
Shift+Tab back; a name with spaces or special characters comes quoted, and
a quoted word completes inside its quotes; after cd, chdir, pushd, rd and
rmdir only directories are offered. The keys are
HKCU/HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Command Processor CompletionChar and
PathCompletionChar (Tab, 0x9, by default; a non-control value such as 0x40
turns it off). The Windows way: ReadConsoleW with a
CONSOLE_READCONSOLE_CONTROL wake-up mask (conhost hands the line back at
the key), the completion, a redraw, and the next read with the completed
text as its initial characters (programs/cmd/complete.c). Gate:
test/cmdcomplete-gate.sh (make test-cmdcomplete), cmd on a pseudo console.
Mutants: SG_MUTANT_NO_COMPLETION, SG_MUTANT_COMPLETE_ANY_AFTER_CD,
SG_MUTANT_COMPLETE_NO_QUOTES.
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/programs/cmd/complete.c
@@ -0,0 +1,296 @@
